 "beats": [
  {
   "type": "title",
   "speaker": "q",
   "scene": "globe",
   "text": "What really destroyed the Spanish Armada?"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "English fireships, English guns, and then the wind."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Why did Spain attack England?",
   "scene": "start",
   "date": "1587",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Queen Elizabeth was Philip's former sister-in-law. She had become his worst enemy."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Her captains, like Francis Drake, raided Spain's treasure fleets. And she sent troops to help the Dutch rebels.",
   "scene": "drake",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Then she executed the Catholic Queen of Scots. Philip called for a crusade.",
   "scene": "maryscots",
   "date": "8 February 1587",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "What was the plan?",
   "scene": "route",
   "date": "May 1588",
   "place": "Lisbon"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The Armada sailed from Lisbon, about a hundred and thirty ships. It would sweep up the Channel, collect an army in Flanders, and land in England."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "At midnight off Calais, the English sent burning ships into the anchored fleet. The Armada scattered in panic.",
   "scene": "fireships",
   "date": "7 August 1588",
   "place": "Calais",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "The next day, at Gravelines, English guns tore into it."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "Couldn't they just sail home?",
   "scene": "flight",
   "date": "Autumn 1588",
   "place": "North Sea"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Not through the Channel. The fleet fled around Scotland and Ireland, and storms smashed dozens of ships on the rocks."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Thousands of men never came home.",
   "scene": "defeat",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.4,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.6,
     0.5,
     1.25
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "How did Philip take it?",
   "scene": "old",
   "date": "",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.4,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.5,
     0.33,
     1.3
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Legend says he only sighed: I sent my ships against men, not against the wind."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And his empire?",
   "scene": "end",
   "date": "1598",
   "place": "Europe"
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Still vast when he died in 1598, but the northern Netherlands were gone for good. And Spain was bankrupt, for the fourth time."
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "a",
   "text": "Next time: Cervantes, the slave who wrote Don Quixote. Like the video and follow History Sketches.",
   "scene": "escorial",
   "move": {
    "from": [
     0.5,
     0.5,
     1.0
    ],
    "to": [
     0.55,
     0.5,
     1.2
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "type": "narration",
   "speaker": "q",
   "text": "And tell us in the comments what you think!"
  },
  {
   "type": "end",
   "text": "Next: Cervantes, the slave who wrote Don Quixote",
